\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Visual understanding results across unified models and self-improvement methods. We apply the same self-evolving recipe to three backbones without changing architecture, data, or reward design. Our method consistently improves all eight visual understanding scores over each base checkpoint, e.g., MMMU $50.6{\to }52.8$ on BLIP3o-8B, $55.3{\to }58.8$ on BAGEL-7B, and $48.6{\to }51.6$ on VARGPT-v1.1. Reasoning-heavy benchmarks show the largest gains (MMMU up to +3.5, MME cognition up to +14.9), while perceptual benchmarks (MMBench, TextVQA) also improve consistently, confirming that self-evolving signals sharpen reasoning without degrading recognition. These improvements emerge from only 6{,}000 unlabeled images and 10k training steps, without any external supervision. Prior methods marked with $\dagger $ use external supervision (e.g., ground-truth labels or external LLMs) and are shown for context as evaluation pipelines differ across methods. Entries marked `--' were not reported by the corresponding source paper.}}{9}{table.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:understanding_results}{{2}{9}{Visual understanding results across unified models and self-improvement methods. We apply the same self-evolving recipe to three backbones without changing architecture, data, or reward design. Our method consistently improves all eight visual understanding scores over each base checkpoint, e.g., MMMU $50.6{\to }52.8$ on BLIP3o-8B, $55.3{\to }58.8$ on BAGEL-7B, and $48.6{\to }51.6$ on VARGPT-v1.1. Reasoning-heavy benchmarks show the largest gains (MMMU up to +3.5, MME cognition up to +14.9), while perceptual benchmarks (MMBench, TextVQA) also improve consistently, confirming that self-evolving signals sharpen reasoning without degrading recognition. These improvements emerge from only 6{,}000 unlabeled images and 10k training steps, without any external supervision. Prior methods marked with $\dagger $ use external supervision (e.g., ground-truth labels or external LLMs) and are shown for context as evaluation pipelines differ across methods. Entries marked `--' were not reported by the corresponding source paper}{table.caption.11}{}}
\newlabel{tab:understanding_results@cref}{{[table][2][]2}{[1][9][]9}{}{}{}}
