\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Image generation results on GenEval across unified models and self-improvement methods. We apply the same self-evolving recipe to three backbones and report six compositional subcategories alongside the overall score. Our method yields a uniform +3\% overall improvement on all three backbones (84\%$\to $87\% on BLIP3o-8B, 82\%$\to $85\% on BAGEL-7B, 53\%$\to $56\% on VARGPT-v1.1), with the largest gains concentrated on composition-heavy subcategories: Two Objects 85\%$\to $93\% and Counting 63\%$\to $71\% on BLIP3o-8B, while already-saturated Single Object (${\geq }96\%$) remains stable. Despite very different absolute baselines, the generation loop adapts to each backbone's current capability without architecture-specific tuning. Prior methods marked with $\dagger $ use external supervision (e.g., ground-truth labels or external LLMs) and are shown for reference as evaluation settings differ across methods. Entries marked `--' were not reported by the corresponding source paper.}}{10}{table.caption.12}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:generation_results}{{3}{10}{Image generation results on GenEval across unified models and self-improvement methods. We apply the same self-evolving recipe to three backbones and report six compositional subcategories alongside the overall score. Our method yields a uniform +3\% overall improvement on all three backbones (84\%$\to $87\% on BLIP3o-8B, 82\%$\to $85\% on BAGEL-7B, 53\%$\to $56\% on VARGPT-v1.1), with the largest gains concentrated on composition-heavy subcategories: Two Objects 85\%$\to $93\% and Counting 63\%$\to $71\% on BLIP3o-8B, while already-saturated Single Object (${\geq }96\%$) remains stable. Despite very different absolute baselines, the generation loop adapts to each backbone's current capability without architecture-specific tuning. Prior methods marked with $\dagger $ use external supervision (e.g., ground-truth labels or external LLMs) and are shown for reference as evaluation settings differ across methods. Entries marked `--' were not reported by the corresponding source paper}{table.caption.12}{}}
\newlabel{tab:generation_results@cref}{{[table][3][]3}{[1][9][]10}{}{}{}}
